            <ArticleTitle>Relationship between pattern of slow-reflow and tissue level of perfusion after coronary stenting: A single-patient report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>222-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Ths study reports different mechanisms (i.e., microvascular spasm and discrete microinfarction) that may underlie different pattern of slow-reflow after elective coronary stenting on the basis of the different tissue level of perfusion achieved, assessed by blush grade and MRI.</AbstractText>
